---
import RecipeLayout from '../../layouts/RecipeLayout.astro';
---
<RecipeLayout title="Brioche Base">
  <div class="recipe-title-block">
    <h1>Brioche Base</h1>
    <p class="subtitle">This one grew up and got a name.</p>
  </div>

  <main>
    <section class="block">
      <div class="callout">
        <p>The Brioche Base is one of the enriched-dough foundations behind Bruce's Breads' Enriched &amp; Sweet section — a stiff, white-flour-leaning levain (45–50% hydration, 40% of flour weight) softened directly into cold milk and eggs before the flour goes in, built specifically to carry butter, sugar, and egg without fighting the dough's structure.</p>
        <p>It's since been given the full recipe treatment, unchanged, shaped the classic French way — a fluted body and a topknot — and published as <a href="/recipes/well-bread/">Well Bread</a>: recipe card, step-by-step tutorial, ingredient history, and a baking playlist. That's the place to go for the complete write-up and the dough this base describes.</p>
        <p>In the meantime, the site's <a href="/guides/">baking Guides</a> have plenty on the technique behind it — the <a href="/guides/starter/starter-vs-levain/">Starter vs. Levain</a> guide covers why this base uses a stiff starter in the first place.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</RecipeLayout>
